From 08e87f3a92c7faac05ab3ec30405c7ad8ec4891a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 06:29:23 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Interface: screens over the game stop the presents between
 its frames

With frame interpolation on, the present thread went on making the
presents between the game's frames while a screen over the paused game
was open: they show the game without the screen, so the window
alternated between the two. The menu stops them before it runs
(hle_media.cpp); the screens over the game now do the same.

- ui/choice_screen: the pause around choose_over_game, notice_over_game
  and type_over_game calls pause_interpolation().
- ui/message_dialog: wait_over_game does too.

Tested with Dissidia 012's port on Windows (clang) at 90 fps: the
chooser, twelve window captures while open and after a move, all show
it; Back returns to the game with interpolation at 90 again. The wait
band in a battle (the other copy frozen for three seconds), eight
captures, all show it; the battle goes on after. Not tested: Linux, the
Steam Deck, Android, another game.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 host/ui/choice_screen.cpp  | 3 +++
 host/ui/message_dialog.cpp | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/host/ui/choice_screen.cpp b/host/ui/choice_screen.cpp
index 9bc9f2c..4b61e6a 100644
--- a/host/ui/choice_screen.cpp
+++ b/host/ui/choice_screen.cpp
@@ -29,6 +29,9 @@ public:
         if (g_depth++ > 0) return;
         Layer &layer = Layer::get();
         stall_watchdog::note_menu(true);
+        // As for the menu: the presents between the game's frames stop, or
+        // they would show the game without the screen between its frames.
+        layer.renderer().pause_interpolation();
         audio::AudioSink::instance().set_paused(true);
         layer.renderer().set_game_input(false);
         layer.set_interactive(true);
diff --git a/host/ui/message_dialog.cpp b/host/ui/message_dialog.cpp
index 1429701..f6d6f3c 100644
--- a/host/ui/message_dialog.cpp
+++ b/host/ui/message_dialog.cpp
@@ -232,6 +232,9 @@ WaitEnd wait_over_game(const std::function<bool(WaitView &)> &step) {
         return WaitEnd::Done;
     }
     stall_watchdog::note_menu(true);
+    // As for the menu: the presents between the game's frames stop, or they
+    // would show the game without the band between its frames.
+    layer.renderer().pause_interpolation();
     audio::AudioSink::instance().set_paused(true);
     layer.renderer().set_game_input(false);
     layer.set_interactive(true);
-- 
